  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 101 AM CDT Sat May 23 2026\n\nA broad upper level trough will be positioned just to our east on \nSunday. Can't rule out a few diurnally driven showers and storms \nin the afternoon with some moisture lingering across our eastern \ncounties but chances are less than 20%. The Memorial Day holiday \nlooks mainly dry with the upper low moving further off to the \neast. Looks like the best chances for showers and thunderstorms \nover the next week will be in the Tuesday/Wednesday time frame. \nModels indicate a stronger disturbance moving across the area \nduring this time frame with the potential for more widespread \nshowers and storms. Thursday into Saturday upper level ridging \nlooks to build back into the region with would result in drier \nconditions but will hold on to at least a slight chance of \nafternoon isolated storms. Otherwise, temperatures look to remain \nnear to slightly below normal through the middle of the week.",
